      "content": "The cycle *is* relentless, and the idea of a small change feeling utterly insignificant is painfully accurate. If you feel that the only true freedom lies in completely opting out, then that feeling of finality must be incredibly strong right now. It's so much easier to see the end as a definitive win when the present feels like an endless, grinding obligation. Please, consider letting someone help you navigate this overwhelming feeling before you make any permanent decisions.",
